            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Exempt in engine/review/app/exempt.go validates the feature as a single safe path segment (review.CheckFeature) and refuses unsafe base/head revisions (review.ErrInvalidRev) before git or the store is touched, so no path traversal or option injection is reachable through the new use case.",
              "The declared risk is gated by review.CheckRisk so anything other than 'none' is refused (high-risk items and unreadable declarations are refused separately), and the report is size-bounded by review.MaxReplyBytes and held to review.CheckReport requiring a clear report; a check that did not run never passes. Enforcement is in the backend use case, not left to the caller.",
              "The candidate is computed from git on every call via s.candidate, the same path as Record, and never taken from the report, so the binding cannot be forged by supplied input; exempt_test.go verifies the git calls match Record's.",
              "service.go changes only parameterize the file-name function passed to store; Record still passes review.ResultName, so its behavior is unchanged. Store still uses exclusive Create with bounded retries and never overwrites an existing file, which exempt_test.go covers.",
              "No secrets, new dependencies, or unsafe input handling are introduced in the four changed files; app.go changes are comment-only."
            ]
          }
        }
