            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths. The Exempt use case in engine/review/app/exempt.go validates the feature, the risk, the report size and the report content before any git or store access, then reuses the same candidate computation and numbered store path as Record. Record's behavior is unchanged: engine/review/app/service.go only threads a name function (review.ResultName) into store.",
              "The tests in engine/review/app/exempt_test.go cover the observable behaviors: the stored file, path, digest and handoff; shared numbering across results, verdicts and exemptions; race and exhaustion retries; high-risk and invalid-risk refusals with no git or store calls; unclear reports; the size boundary at exactly MaxReplyBytes and one byte over; unsafe feature and revision values; git and store failures; the not-flushed case; and Record regression coverage next to an existing exemption.",
              "I found no reliability defect introduced by this candidate. The helpers it depends on (review.CheckRisk, review.CheckReport, review.EncodeExemption, review.ExemptionName, review.ExemptionHandoff) are outside the visible scope, so I did not assess them."
            ]
          }
